    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with **BUILD SUCCESS** (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the deterministic `householdId` change in the PetClinic Spring Boot app. The work centered on three areas:\n\n**1. `householdIdFor(Owner)` \u2014 now deterministic from (lastName, postcode)** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- Changed the hash input from `normalizedLastName + '|' + normalizedAddress` to `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`.\n- Changed the output from 24 hex chars (12 bytes) to the **first 12 hex characters** (6 bytes) of SHA-256, per spec.\n\n**2. `householdMembers(Owner)` \u2014 keyed on the computed householdId**\n- Now matches existing owners by equal `householdIdFor(...)` rather than by comparing last name + address, so duplicate detection and the household-size calculation both key off the same computed id.\n\n**3. `addOwner(...)` flow rewrite**\n- `householdId` is now **always assigned deterministically** on create (`owner.setHouseholdId(householdIdFor(owner))`), instead of only being copied from an existing member when `sharesHousehold` was set.\n- Removed the old link-propagation block that back-filled other members' ids.\n- Added a **household-duplicate 409**: when another owner already shares the (lastName, postcode) household, the create is rejected \u2014 **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set, which now *only bypasses this block*.\n- A **declared household member** (`sharesHousehold` + existing members) is explicitly **not flagged as a possible duplicate** (`possibleDuplicate=false`), matching \"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\"\n- Kept the exact `identityKey` (telephone|email|householdId) match as a hard-duplicate guard.\n\n**4. Docs** \u2014 updated the `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to reflect the new deterministic/bypass semantics.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) confirms the observable contract: same lastName+postcode \u2192 same `householdId` (via the `sharesHousehold` bypass), and a different lastName \u2192 a different `householdId`.",
